# Runtime environment for the Campus ERP container.
# Copy to .env.server and fill in. Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# Two different groups matter:
#   VITE_*  -> inlined into the browser bundle at `docker compose build` time.
#              Changing one needs a rebuild, not just a restart.
#   others  -> read by the Node server at runtime (restart is enough).

# --- Build time: browser-visible, safe to expose -----------------------------
# Leave empty to keep the values already committed in the repo's .env.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Runtime: server process only --------------------------------------------
# Same project as above; used by SSR routes and server functions.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Grants bypass-all RLS access. Keep it out of every VITE_* variable, or it
# ships inside publicly downloadable JavaScript.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Runtime: tuning ---------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=3000
# NODE_LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- Runtime: attendance persistence -----------------------------------------
# The server picks one store at boot and reports it on the teacher page:
#   1. Supabase  — SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY below, and the tables
#                  from supabase/migrations/20260930090000_attendance_mirror_tables.sql
#   2. JSON file — DATA_DIR/attendance.json, when the database is not configured
#                  and this directory is writable
#   3. none      — neither works: *Start live QR* refuses, and says what is missing
#
# On a serverless host (Vercel) the code directory is read-only and every instance
# gets its own ephemeral disk, so option 2 cannot ever share a session between two
# devices. There, SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are not optional: without
# them attendance has no store and no session can start.
# DATA_DIR=/data        # already /data in the image (eqr-data volume)

# When the JSON file is the live store and these credentials are also present, every
# write is mirrored into the same erp_* tables as a best-effort copy — a mirror
# failure logs a warning and never blocks or fakes a mark.
#
# Values still containing the word "placeholder" are treated as unset, so the
# committed offline-mode defaults cannot silently look configured. Publishable keys
# alone are never enough: RLS on erp_attendance_* grants access to service_role only.
